WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.630
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.860
Phobophobia is an intense fear of developing
a phobia.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:19.550
When you are born you only have two fears,
a fear of falling and loud noises.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:25.090
These are natural survival mechanisms built
into our DNA and passed down through the generations.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.230
Every other fear you face, you have learnt
throughout your life.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:34.710
Dikephobia is a fear of justice and Eleutherophobia
is a fear of freedom.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:40.520
You'll have to stay clear of the Netherlands
if you have Dutchphobia, a fear of the Dutch.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.370
Euphobia is a fear of hearing good news, but
don't tell them there's a cure.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:51.090
Some phobias can be unexplainably bizarre,
such as Levophobia which is a fear of things

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.140
to the left of your body.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.829
Lutraphobia is a fear of otters.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:01:01.109
Did you know that otters hold hands whilst
sleeping so they don't drift away from each.

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:04.820
How can something so otterly adorable be scary.a

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.440
Pentheraphobia is a fear of your mother-in-law.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:13.620
One New Scientist reader discovered a telephone
helpline dedicated to helping those with a

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:19.620
variety of ailments, one of these was Telephonophobia,
a fear of telephones.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.510
Xanthophobia is the fear of the colour yellow.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:29.330
Xanthophobics can be afraid of the sun, daffodils,
yellow paint, and many other yellow objects.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:36.080
In some aggressive cases of Xanthophobia,
sufferers are even afraid of the word "yellow".

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.960
Somniphobia is a fear of falling asleep.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.530
Somniphobes fear falling asleep because they
associate it with dying.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:48.350
It can also be related to a feeling of lack
of control or from suffering repeated nightmares.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:53.070
Some Somniphobes are simply scared of losing
time whilst sleeping.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.840
Think that's difficult to live with?

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.470
It's not as bad as Phronemophobia.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.410
Phronemophobia is a fear of thinking.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:04.140
Nomophobia is the fear of being without mobile
phone coverage.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.989
It may sound ridiculous but it has been well
observed by researchers and is actually one

00:02:08.989 --> 00:02:10.310
of the biggest phobias.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:16.680
A survey in the UK revealed that 54% of Britons
suffer from Nomophobia.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:22.670
Suffers fear losing signal, running out of
battery or simply losing sight of their phone.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.640
Papaphobia is a rare fear of the Pope or Papacy.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:32.980
It is closely related to Hierophobia, a fear
of holy individuals or sacred objects.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.840
It is usually related to a traumatic experience
associated with the Pope.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.209
Pogonophobia is a strong fear of beards.

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:44.389
The term has been used since the 1850s.

00:02:44.389 --> 00:02:51.049
British journalist Jeremy Paxman recently
accused the BBC of suffering from Pogonophobia

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:56.170
after he was criticised for sporting a beard
whilst presenting Newsnight.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:00.030
Similarly, Peladophobia is a fear of bald
people.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:06.370
But the cruelest phobia of all is Hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.310
This ironically named phobia is the fear of
long words.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.010
Now that's just mean.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:18.340
Suffers of Hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia
are scared of the name of their own phobia.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:24.701
And finally Anatidaephobia is the fear that
wherever you are, whatever you're doing, there

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:27.129
is a duck watching you.

00:03:27.129 --> 00:03:30.870
Unfortunately the fear isn't real, it was
made up by Gary Larson.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:40.010
But that hasn't stopped many people from believing
there are actual sufferers of Anatidaephobia.

